    "findings": [
      "The restore authority constructor checks package/export labels and callable shape, but that does not establish executable provenance. Every restore decision must return exact numeric 1 or -1 and agree with locally established presence/integrity; exceptions, unknown values and disagreement refuse. Successful restoration still re-verifies integrity in deserialize, so preserve ordering and provider-call count.",
      "StateSerializer must preserve UTF-8 encoding, unsigned 32-bit XOR folding, exact delimiter-separated HMAC input, SHA-256, lowercase 64-character hexadecimal validation, safe-integer bounds, keyId restrictions and constant-time MAC comparison. JSON behavior is material: toJSON/getters can execute, unsupported top-level values receive the explicit snapshot error, cycles/BigInt can throw native exceptions, and verification authenticates payloadJson without establishing valid JSON.",
      "Key custody: default mode accepts the development zero key; strict mode rejects weak supplied keys. A provider with no active key can construct successfully but serialization refuses. Historical snapshots remain valid while their epoch resolves; no logical-tick monotonicity or replay-prevention gate exists. Provider effects, revocation between the two verification calls and mutable key handles require explicit assumptions.",
      "AtomicWriter joins names directly into paths without containment validation; traversal and symlink custody are unresolved. Writes reuse a predictable .tmp name without locking or exclusive creation and do not fsync file or directory, so power-loss durability is unproven.",
      "scrub zero-writes and unlinks one live path, without durable flush or proof of physical-media erasure; snapshots, journaling, flash wear-leveling, permissions and failures remain host seams.",
      "Existing Fungi assets fold the two-Boolean restore verdict and four String constants only. They do not replace JSON, HMAC, key custody, atomic storage, scrub guarantees or orchestration. The four constant assets cite an obsolete packages-galerina oracle prefix. RD-0361 proves bounded decision folds and selected restore vectors, not complete persistence/crypto parity.",
      "ARCHITECTURE_ISSUES.md understates the implementation by describing only a fixed key and deferred key-ID stamping; source now implements epoch providers and authenticates epoch identity. Encryption-at-rest and actual engine-state extraction remain external obligations."
    ],
    "materialObligations": [
      "Preserve authority identity/provenance, exact numeric verdicts, local-fact agreement, verify-before-deserialize, double-verification and error ordering.",
      "Preserve UTF-8, XOR/HMAC framing, key/epoch custody, JSON side effects, strict-key defaults and provider mutation/rotation behavior.",
      "Preserve path containment, atomic write/rename, concurrency, durability, scrub and host filesystem failure semantics or explicitly narrow the host contract.",
      "Keep all five Fungi assets non-authorizing, correct obsolete oracle provenance under a separate documentation scope, and retain TypeScript shadow until separately admitted replacement proof exists."
    ]
  },
